**Concrete Correction:**
- Before merging any PR or change
- After completing a feature implementation
- When another agent or model produced code you need to evaluate
- When refactoring existing code
- After any bug fix (review both the fix and the regression test)

**Regression Example:**
Before merging a PR, ensure that the regression test for the new functionality is complete and passing. If the regression test fails, it indicates that the new feature has introduced a regression. For example:

```typescript
// Before merging
function checkFeature() {
  // Regression test code
  const items = [{ name: 'Test Item' }];
  const first = items[0].name; // items may be empty
  console.log(first); // Should log 'Test Item'
}

// After merging
function checkFeature() {
  // Regression test code
  const items = [{ name: 'Test Item' }];
  const first = items[0].name; // items may be empty
  console.log(first); // Should log 'Test Item'
}
```
